      "value": "@{5f2dc3d9b923f7086bb0a2b5|full_name}: Yeah, network-instantiating stuff is somehow a feature in the client and I don't understand why. The real solution is to not even have an endpoint on the client for unsupported \"features\" like that. Why accepting a remote change of a pedestal at all if this isn't even a game related feature? No endpoint, no problem :)",
