  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-14T11:51:42.184Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A modified client user was able to overwrite an avatar pedestal in our world (change the avatar ID for others) and other users see the same issue happening as well in their world. Example: https://twitter.com/EngineerNeet/status/1380573991845253122\nIt's already a security issue that there is even the possibility to do \"unsupported\" things like remotely changing a pedestal or instantiating stuff on other clients.\nSuch hidden \"features\" are only an invitation for client users to do malicious stuff. Ideally, the client would be hardened and not support anything that isn't needed today to leave no place for modded clients to exploit those.",
